       <h1>Aaryavir Sehwag's Century Powers India in U19 Asia Cup Clash Against UAE</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Cricket</span> <span>#U19 Asia Cup</span> <span>#India</span> <span>#UAE</span></div>
       <p>Aaryavir Sehwag's century has propelled India into a commanding position against the UAE in their U19 Asia Cup Group A match held in Oman. Sehwag reached his triple figures off 131 balls, an innings that included 13 fours and two sixes. Earlier in the match, UAE captain Ayaan Misbah won the toss and elected to bowl first.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-10/aaryavir-sehwags-century-powers-india-in-u19-asia-cup-clash-.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>India entered this crucial encounter following a three-wicket defeat to arch-rivals Pakistan. The victor of today's match will secure a spot in the semi-finals, joining Pakistan, Afghanistan, and Bangladesh. There was particular focus on Aaryavir Sehwag and Anvay Dravid, both of whom had failed to make significant scores against Pakistan, and were eager for redemption against the UAE. Sehwag made his intentions clear early on, scoring 21 runs off one Uddish Suri over with a sequence of 4, 6, 4, 6, which put India firmly on track for a score nearing 300.</p><p>Sehwag had earlier completed his half-century with a six off 69 balls, marking his second fifty of the tournament. The Indian innings saw moments of strong partnerships, including a 50-run stand. However, boundaries dried up for 21 balls at one point, with UAE spinners successfully pegging India back, as VK Vineeth struggled to get going and Aaryavir adopted a more cautious approach after his fifty. The team's score progressed steadily, reaching 196/1 in 37 overs, 175-1 in 36 overs, and 159/1 when Sehwag completed his century in 33.5 overs.</p><p>India's innings began with some early challenges. Captain Lakshya Raichandani was dismissed for 17 runs off 32 balls at 62/1 after 13.5 overs. Aaryavir Sehwag himself faced a real struggle initially, taking 14 balls to open his account. He was also given two reprieves, surviving a dropped catch at 69/1 after 15.5 overs. Despite these early hurdles, Sehwag's aggressive and composed play, including early boundaries and aerial shots, ensured India remained in control.</p><p>What to watch: India's performance in the semi-finals after securing their spot.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The report is comprehensive and accurately synthesizes the live updates into a cohesive narrative, correctly capturing the match flow and key statistics.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://sports.ndtv.com/cricket/india-vs-uae-u19-live-score-ind-vs-uae-u19-asia-cup-2026-live-updates-aaryavir-sehwag-anvay-dravid-12305796#publisher=newsstand" rel="noopener">NDTV Sports</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
