     <article class="story single" data-beat="cricket">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">CRICKET</span> · Crictracker · 2026-11-10 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Adelaide Strikers Clinch Last-Ball Thriller Against Hobart Hurricanes in WBBL 2026</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Cricket</span> <span>#WBBL</span> <span>#Adelaide Strikers</span> <span>#Hobart Hurricanes</span></div>
       <p>Adelaide Strikers secured a dramatic four-wicket victory over Hobart Hurricanes in Match 17 of the 2026 Women's Big Bash League at Bellerive Oval in Hobart on November 10. Chasing a target of 139, Sophie Ecclestone delivered the decisive blow, striking the winning boundary off the very last ball of the innings. This hard-fought win elevated Adelaide's season record to 2-2.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-10/adelaide-strikers-clinch-last-ball-thriller-against-hobart-h.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The painful last-ball defeat further extended Hobart's winless run to five matches in the competition. This loss followed a similarly tight defeat to Melbourne Renegades, which also involved a no-ball controversy, marking two consecutive last-ball defeats for the Hurricanes. In their innings, Hobart set a total of 138 for 6, with skipper Nicola Carey anchoring the score, finishing unbeaten on 66 off 53 balls. Wickets fell at regular intervals around Carey, as Chamari Athapaththu scored 10 off 26 balls before being retired out, and Lizelle Lee made 19 off 18 balls before being trapped leg-before by Ecclestone. Rachel Trenaman was dismissed caught-and-bowled for 9 runs, with middle-order contributions helping them reach their competitive total.</p><p>Adelaide Strikers' chase was characterized by contributions from multiple batters. Maia Bouchier provided early momentum, striking 26 off 19 balls. Emma de Broughe then played a measured knock of 41 off 37 balls, crucial for keeping Adelaide in contention through the middle overs. Laura Wolvaardt added 27 off 27 balls but was caught off the fifth-last delivery, tightening the equation significantly. With four runs still required off the final ball, Ecclestone, who had earlier contributed with the ball by returning figures of 1 for 37 including the key dismissal of Lee, stepped up to hit the boundary and complete the win.</p><p>What to watch: Hobart will be under pressure to find a winning formula in their upcoming fixtures.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurate, detailed sports report utilizing all available match statistics from the source.</p>
