       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">TECH</span> · The Verge · 2026-11-10 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Anthropic Targets $1.4 Trillion Valuation in Upcoming IPO</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#tech</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Anthropic confirmed on Tuesday that its initial public offering is expected to price between $70.00 and $78.00 per share, targeting a valuation of up to $1.4 trillion. The company has applied to list its Class A common stock on the Nasdaq Global Select Market under the symbol ANT, with shares potentially trading next Thursday or Friday. Although the valuation falls short of prior expectations reaching up to $2 trillion, the offering stands to be one of the largest in history.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-10/anthropic-targets-14-trillion-valuation-in-upcoming-ipo.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async">
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately reports the figures and details provided in the source text.</p>
