       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">BUSINESS</span> · Economic Times · 2026-11-10 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Democrat Mary Peltola Expands Alaska Senate Lead</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#business</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Democrat Mary Peltola has widened her lead over Republican incumbent Dan Sullivan in the uncalled Alaska Senate race. Following a Monday update from the Alaska Division of Elections, Peltola holds a 2,517-vote advantage, securing 48.6% of the first-choice vote compared to Sullivan's 47.5%.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-10/democrat-mary-peltola-expands-alaska-senate-lead.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Thousands of ballots remain uncounted, with further updates expected on November 10 and 13. Because no candidate has exceeded 50% of the first-choice vote, a ranked-choice tabulation is scheduled for November 18. The current results remain unofficial until the final count is completed and the redistribution process occurs.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief effectively synthesizes the key metrics and context of the election status provided in the source.</p>
