     <article class="story single" data-beat="finance">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">FINANCE</span> · Livemint Money · 2026-11-10 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>EPFO outlines five-step online process to correct EPF account details</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#finance</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The Employees’ Provident Fund Organisation (EPFO) has reminded members that incorrect personal or employment details can delay claim settlements, balance transfers, or withdrawals. To resolve discrepancies in names, dates of birth, or gender, members can utilize the online Joint Declaration facility available on the official EPFO Member Portal.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-10/epfo-outlines-five-step-online-process-to-correct-epf-accoun.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The correction process involves logging in with a Universal Account Number, selecting the Joint Declaration facility, identifying the incorrect fields, and uploading supporting documents such as Aadhaar or birth certificates. Once submitted, the requests undergo verification to ensure records remain accurate and aligned with official documentation.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief clearly outlines the purpose and five-step process for the EPFO correction facility.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.livemint.com/money/personal-finance/wrong-details-in-pf-account-can-delay-your-money-epfo-explains-how-to-correct-them-online-in-5-easy-steps-11794293434161.html" rel="noopener">Livemint Money</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
