       <h1>Hampshire House Martins Project Expands Artificial Nest Initiative</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#science</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The Hampshire House Martins Project is expanding its conservation efforts by installing up to 900 free artificial nest cups for the endangered UK bird species. These woodcrete nests provide a durable, ready-made alternative to mud nests, which birds struggle to construct due to insect declines, hotter weather, and modern uPVC building materials. Following a successful pilot where 249 cups were installed, the group is now seeking properties within 1km of previous nest sites.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-10/hampshire-house-martins-project-expands-artificial-nest-init.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>UK house martin populations have plummeted 40% since 1995 due to poor breeding success and habitat challenges. The project aims to provide safe nesting sites for birds returning from Africa each spring, supporting their recovery.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Concise and accurate reporting of the initiative's scope and the environmental factors driving the decline.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
