       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">DEFENCE</span> · Defence (aggregate) · 2026-11-10 · editor 7/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>India Orders Eight Project 28A Corvettes for Indian Ocean Trade Security</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#India</span> <span>#Defence</span> <span>#Corvettes</span> <span>#Indian Ocean</span></div>
       <p>India has formally placed an order for eight Project 28A Corvettes, as reported by Defence Security Asia. This strategic acquisition represents a significant expansion of the nation's naval assets and maritime defence infrastructure.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-10/india-orders-eight-project-28a-corvettes-for-indian-ocean-tr.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The primary role designated for these eight Project 28A Corvettes is to guard Indian Ocean trade. This directive highlights India's focused effort to enhance security along critical commercial shipping routes within the Indian Ocean region, ensuring stability for vital trade flows.</p><p>What to watch: Details regarding the manufacturing timeline and deployment strategy for these corvettes.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: A concise and accurate wire item that exhausts the very brief source material without unwarranted padding.</p>
