     <article class="story single" data-beat="sports">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">SPORTS</span> · NDTV Sports · 2026-11-10 · editor 9/10 · 2 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Indian Boxers Meetei, Gunjan Assure Medals at Youth Olympics</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Youth Olympics</span> <span>#Boxing</span> <span>#Badminton</span> <span>#India</span></div>
       <p>Indian boxer Lairenlakpam Ambekar Meetei has assured India of a medal at the Youth Olympic Games by advancing to the semifinals of the men's 50kg category. On Tuesday, Meetei secured a dominant victory over Namibia's Abraham Kalenga via Referee Stopped Contest (RSC) in the opening round of their quarterfinal bout, which concluded after 1 minute and 57 seconds. Meetei is scheduled to face Colombia's Izzon Jeffrey Arevalo in the semifinal on Wednesday.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-10/indian-boxers-meetei-gunjan-assure-medals-at-youth-olympics.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Adding to India's medal prospects, boxer Gunjan also assured the country of a medal by defeating Mexico's Atena Sofia Juarez Calero with a 5-0 score to reach the semifinals. With these two victories, India has now guaranteed at least a bronze medal from both Meetei and Gunjan, further increasing the nation's tally at the Games, which already includes three silver and five bronze medals.</p><p>Meanwhile, fifteen-year-old Indian badminton sensation Tanvi Patri has adjusted her expectations following a series of injuries. Her primary goal for the next two years is now to qualify for the 2028 Los Angeles Olympics.</p><p>Fresh from securing a silver medal at the Youth Olympics in Dakar, Tanvi also aims to win the Asian Junior Championships and World Junior Championships, alongside breaking into the top-30 of the world rankings. Her budding career has seen her contend with knee, hamstring, and most recently, a back injury. She stated, &quot;Like earlier I used to say that my aim is to get a medal for my country in LA. But now, like this year also I had back injury. And last year also I had hamstring injury. So, I think my aim is to like to qualify for LA and play my best there for now.&quot; She acknowledged the difficulty in qualifying but affirmed her determination. For the upcoming year, her specific goals include winning the Asian Under-19 Junior Championships and the World Junior Championships. Tanvi's health issues also impacted her performance at the world juniors last month.</p><p>What to watch: Meetei and Gunjan's semifinal bouts and Tanvi Patri's journey toward the 2028 Los Angeles Olympics.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The report accurately synthesizes the boxing results and the update on Tanvi Patri's career trajectory.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://sports.ndtv.com/boxing/lairenlakpam-ambekar-meetei-assures-india-of-medal-at-youth-olympics-12308708#publisher=newsstand" rel="noopener">NDTV Sports</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
