     <article class="story single" data-beat="world">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">WORLD</span> · The Hindu World · 2026-11-10 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>NMDC Explores Russian Lithium Investment Opportunities</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#world</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Indian state-run miner NMDC Ltd. has entered preliminary talks with Russia's Rosatom to explore lithium mining and processing investments. NMDC officials visited Russia last month to discuss potential partnerships as India seeks to secure critical mineral supplies for its growing battery and EV industries.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-10/nmdc-explores-russian-lithium-investment-opportunities.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>While India currently relies on imports for lithium, it is diversifying its mineral strategy through global acquisitions and domestic incentives. Meanwhile, Russia is developing its largest lithium deposit through the PolarLithium joint venture between Rosatom and Nornickel, targeting commercial production by 2030. NMDC has also reportedly held discussions with other Russian companies regarding potential mineral assets.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurate summary of the investment talks and context, though it omits the Rosatom spokesperson's denial mentioned in the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/business/nmdc-said-to-be-in-talks-with-russias-rosatom-over-lithium-investments/article71687322.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu World</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
