      <a href="/feed.xml" title="RSS">RSS</a>
      <button id="tdp-theme" title="Toggle light/dark">Light</button>
    </div>
  </div>
  <nav class="catrow"><span class="catgrp"><b>News</b><a href="/category/national">national</a><a href="/category/world">world</a><a href="/category/defence">defence</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Money</b><a href="/category/business">business</a><a href="/category/finance">finance</a><a href="/category/education">education</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Sports</b><a href="/category/sports">sports</a><a href="/category/cricket">cricket</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Culture</b><a href="/category/entertainment">entertainment</a><a href="/category/positive">positive</a><a href="/category/funny">funny</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Life</b><a href="/category/science">science</a><a href="/category/environment">environment</a><a href="/category/space">space</a><a href="/category/health">health</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Tech</b><a href="/category/tech">tech</a><a href="/category/ai">ai</a></span></nav></div><div class="gtr"><span>Read in your language:</span><div id="google_translate_element"></div></div><div class="wrap"><main id="content"><p class="crumb"><a href="/">← Front page</a> · <a href="/archive">Archive</a> · <a href="/category/national">national</a></p>
     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · India Today · 2026-11-10 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Punjab Records 198 New Farm Fires, Total Exceeds 4,600 Despite Warnings</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#National</span> <span>#Punjab</span> <span>#Farm Fires</span> <span>#Pollution</span></div>
       <p>Punjab recorded 198 fresh farm fires on Monday, increasing the total number of such incidents to 4,657 during the monitoring period, according to news agency Press Trust of India. This rise occurs despite government advisories against burning crop residue, with Tarn Taran, Ferozepur, and Sangrur reporting the highest number of cases.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-10/punjab-records-198-new-farm-fires-total-exceeds-4600-despite.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Official data indicates that Tarn Taran registered 659 farm fires, followed by Ferozepur with 621, Sangrur with 508, Bathinda with 412, Patiala with 299, and Amritsar with 247. In response to these violations, authorities have imposed fines totaling Rs 72.85 lakh in 1,442 cases, of which Rs 33.60 lakh has been recovered so far, PTI reported.</p><p>Further action includes the registration of 938 First Information Reports (FIRs) under Section 223 of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, which addresses disobedience of an order issued by a public servant. Additionally, state authorities have made 1,150 'red entries' in the land records of farmers who burnt crop residue. These include 310 entries in Tarn Taran and 192 in Ferozepur, with a red entry preventing farmers from securing loans against their farmland or selling it.</p><p>The annual monitoring of farm fires commences on September 15, two weeks before paddy procurement begins on October 1. Stubble burning in Punjab and Haryana is frequently cited as a significant contributor to increased air pollution in Delhi-NCR. Farmers often resort to burning fields to quickly clear crop residue, allowing them sufficient time to sow wheat after the paddy harvest in October and November. In previous years, Punjab recorded 5,114 farm fires in the 2025 paddy harvesting season, 10,909 in 2024, and 36,663 in 2023.</p><p>What to watch: The effectiveness of ongoing enforcement measures against farm fires.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft accurately reports the data provided in the source text, including regional breakdowns, enforcement statistics, and historical comparisons.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.indiatoday.in/india/punjab/story/punjab-farm-fires-reach-4657-fines-firs-red-entries-ptag-3035893-2026-11-10?utm_source=rss" rel="noopener">India Today</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
