       <h1>Sonia Gandhi Officially Confirms Cancer Treatment History in Memoirs</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>In her new memoirs, 'Belonging: A Journey of Love,' Sonia Gandhi has publicly confirmed her battle with cancer during the UPA government's second term. Contrary to long-standing speculation, she received treatment at the European Institute of Oncology in Italy for breast cancer and at Erasmus University Medical Centre in Rotterdam for a pancreatic growth. Both surgeries were attended by her children, Rahul and Priyanka.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-10/sonia-gandhi-officially-confirms-cancer-treatment-history-in.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Gandhi also detailed a 2016 incident where she collapsed during a Varanasi roadshow, resulting in a broken shoulder. She noted that during the flight to Delhi, she experienced a vision of her late husband, Rajiv Gandhi, which provided her with reassurance.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurately details the memoir's revelations regarding Gandhi's cancer treatment and the 2016 incident.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/for-the-first-time-sonia-confirms-battle-with-cancer-in-memoirs/articleshow/135719721.cms" rel="noopener">Times of India</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
