       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-11-10 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Telangana SAFE defends restaurant suspensions amid safety concerns</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Telangana SAFE Commissioner Avinash Mohanty defended the suspension of select Hyderabad restaurants, stating such measures were necessary when food safety hazards were found to be extreme. This clarification follows a meeting with a delegation of restaurant owners, led by MP Asaduddin Owaisi, who requested improvement notices and time to rectify minor deficiencies before facing license suspensions.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-10/telangana-safe-defends-restaurant-suspensions-amid-safety-co.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Mohanty emphasized that uniform guidelines are applied to all inspections to prevent preferential treatment. While some establishments faced license cancellations, most received improvement or show-cause notices. Owners acknowledged the importance of cleanliness, while officials maintained that public safety remains the priority for severe violations.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately summarizes the meeting between restaurant owners and the Commissioner regarding enforcement procedures.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/cities/Hyderabad/only-few-hyderabad-eateries-faced-suspension-most-received-improvement-notices-telangana-safe/article71685117.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
