     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-11-10 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Three family members killed in Madhya Pradesh house collapse</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Three people were killed and four others injured when a mud house collapsed in the Jalhathani Tola area of Singrauli, Madhya Pradesh, on Monday night. The victims, identified as 36-year-old Arun Vishwakarma, his 65-year-old mother Satuliya Devi, and his two-year-old daughter, were sleeping when the structure suddenly crumbled.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-10/three-family-members-killed-in-madhya-pradesh-house-collapse.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Local police and district officials utilized an excavator to rescue the trapped family members. The injured were transported to a private hospital for treatment. Villagers confirmed the family had been receiving financial assistance under the Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojana for the construction of a new home at the time of the tragedy.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately reports the casualty numbers, victim identities, and the context regarding the PMAY assistance.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/madhya-pradesh/three-members-of-family-killed-four-injured-as-house-collapses-in-mps-singrauli/article71685352.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
