     <article class="story single" data-beat="education">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">EDUCATION</span> · Education (aggregate) · 2026-11-10 · editor 7/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>University of Hyderabad to Organise Free Higher Education Leadership Training</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Education</span> <span>#Hyderabad</span> <span>#Leadership Training</span></div>
       <p>The University of Hyderabad is preparing to organise a training programme on higher education leadership and governance. This upcoming initiative focuses on enhancing skills and understanding within the academic administration sector.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-10/university-of-hyderabad-to-organise-free-higher-education-le.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Notably, the programme is entirely free, making it accessible to a wide range of participants. It specifically targets key areas of leadership and governance essential for effective management in higher education.</p><p>This development was reported by The Indian Express. The university's move underscores a commitment to fostering better leadership practices across educational institutions.</p><p>What to watch: Further announcements regarding programme dates and eligibility.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurately covers the brief source summary without unnecessary fabrication.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://news.google.-?oc=5" rel="noopener">Education (aggregate)</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
